{"voiceId": "kokoro_am_adam", "modelId": "kokoro-v0_19_local", "sampleRate": 44100, "scenes": [{"id": "vo", "text": "Sixty-six million years ago, dinosaurs ruled the Earth as undisputed apex predators, an unbroken reign spanning over one hundred and sixty million years. From deep space, a mountain-sized asteroid ten kilometers wide hurtled toward Earth at forty-five thousand miles per hour. The impact in the Yucatan unleashed the fury of one hundred million megatons, triggering apocalyptic megatsunamis hundreds of meters high. Shockwaves fractured the Earth's mantle, triggering the Deccan Traps supervolcanoes and pumping billions of tons of toxic sulfur into the skies. A suffocating blanket of soot blotted out the sun for a decade. Global temperatures plummeted, photosynthesis halted, and the food chain collapsed. Seventy-five percent of all species vanished forever, leaving a thin layer of cosmic iridium... and sparking the dawn of the age of mammals.", "wav": "vo.wav", "duration": 50.7086, "speechStart": 0.45, "speechEnd": 50.296, "words": [{"id": "w0", "text": "Sixty-six", "start": 0.45, "end": 0.932}, {"id": "w1", "text": "million", "start": 0.997, "end": 1.419}, {"id": "w2", "text": "years", "start": 1.476, "end": 1.777}, {"id": "w3", "text": "ago,", "start": 1.819, "end": 2.09}, {"id": "w4", "text": "dinosaurs", "start": 2.126, "end": 2.668}, {"id": "w5", "text": "ruled", "start": 2.742, "end": 3.043}, {"id": "w6", "text": "the", "start": 3.084, "end": 3.265}, {"id": "w7", "text": "Earth", "start": 3.29, "end": 3.591}, {"id": "w8", "text": "as", "start": 3.632, "end": 3.752}, {"id": "w9", "text": "undisputed", "start": 3.769, "end": 4.371}, {"id": "w10", "text": "apex", "start": 4.453, "end": 4.694}, {"id": "w11", "text": "predators,", "start": 4.727, "end": 5.359}, {"id": "w12", "text": "an", "start": 5.445, "end": 5.566}, {"id": "w13", "text": "unbroken", "start": 5.582, "end": 6.064}, {"id": "w14", "text": "reign", "start": 6.129, "end": 6.431}, {"id": "w15